[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4210738595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118334#issuecomment-4210738595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118334","id":4210738595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76-sWj","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T00:59:32Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T01:08:19Z","body":"Hi, thank you for your report! This is a little known bug I didn't have the chance to fix yet. This is caused by duplicate mouse enter and mouse exit events. We just need to have better state tracking, which I'll work on soon™.\n\nThat said, I've never seen the warning about exit events on sway, I think. I wonder if it's somewhat related to #114238 where certain compositors emit leave events while others don't. I assume you're replicating this on muffin, as per our last discussion?\n\nThat crash is news to me. From a very quick glance it's trying to access the root of the window, which I suppose has been destroyed. There should probably be a `ERR_FAIL_NULL` as a safeguard but we can definitely ensure that this does not happen.\n\nEdit: to be clear: *mouse* enter/exit events are Godot `WindowEvent`s, while pointer enter/leave events are Wayland events. It's a bit ambiguous, sorry, hope the point went across 😅 ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4210738595/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4210766694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118334#issuecomment-4210766694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118334","id":4210766694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76-zNm","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T01:08:45Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T01:33:48Z","body":"> Hi, thank you for your report! This is a little known bug I didn't have the chance to fix yet. This is caused by duplicate mouse enter and mouse exit events. We just need to have better state tracking, which I'll work on soon™.\n\nIt's great to hear that, and thank you for your work.\n\n> That said, I've never seen exit events on sway, I think. I wonder if it's somewhat related to [#114238](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114238) where certain compositors emit leave events while others don't. I assume you're replicating this on muffin, as per our last discussion?\n\nReproducible on both Muffin and Sway (1.9). Moreover, there are no errors similar to those reported in #114238.\n\n> That crash is news to me. From a very quick glance it's trying to access the root of the window, which I suppose has been destroyed. There should probably be a `ERR_FAIL_NULL` as a safeguard but we can definitely ensure that this does not happen.\n\nDuring the attempted reproduction, this crash occurred only once. It may require certain other conditions.\n\nEdit:\n\nIncidentally, I also tested launching with `GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_LIBDECOR=1`. It is still reproducible. Not reproducible on v4.7.dev3.official [60fff00a6] (must be launched with `GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_LIBDECOR=1`).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4210766694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4359794834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118334#issuecomment-4359794834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118334","id":4359794834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA90wkg","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.githu